#      REACTION                                      ALPHA         BETA    GAMMA  REF     (added by JRB)
Reactions included in the STAND2020 chemical network,
compiled from Sources (A) and (B).

Source (A):
================================================================================
Title: A Chemical Kinetics Network for Lightning 
       and Life in Planetary Atmospheres 
Authors: Rimmer P.B., Helling C. 
Table: Stand2015 Chemical Kinetics Network
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Source (B):
================================================================================
Title: Hydroxide salts in the clouds of Venus: their effect on the 
       sulfur cycle and cloud droplet
Authors: Rimmer P.B., Jordan S., Constantinou T., Woitke P., Shorttle O., 
         Hobbs R., Paschodimas A. 
Table: Reactions Added and Updated for STAND2020
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

================================================================================
Byte-by-byte Description of file
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Bytes Format Units   Label     Explanations
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   1- 51 A38    ---     Reaction  Reaction
  52- 59 E8.2   ---     alpha     The {alpha} value
  61- 65 A5     ---   u_alpha     alpha units
  67- 72 F5.2   ---     beta      The {beta} value
  74- 81 F7.1   K       Ea        Ea (1)
  83- 86 A21    ---     Ref       Reference (2)
  87- 89 A3     ---     Flag      Flag (3)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Note (1): Rate-constants --
    Rate constants for two-body reactions are calculated from alpha, beta, and 
    gamma according to the Kooij equation, with temperature normalised by 300K 
    in the beta term (consult Source (A): Section 2.1 on how the reaction 
    barrier is calculated). 

    Rate constants for reactions involving a third body follow the Lindemann 
    form. The reaction is first listed in the the network with alpha, beta, and 
    gamma values that correspond to the rate-constant in the low-pressure limit. 
    The reaction is then repeated with alpha, beta, and gamma values that 
    correspond to the rate-constant in the high-pressure limit (consult Source(A): 
    Section 2.2 on how the reaction barrier is calculated).

    * = Consult Source (A): Section 2.3 on how the reaction barrier is calculated.

